@XFDG Thanks for catching this. I confirmed the forced overwrite in `_ensure_main_grad` and removed that assignment. The helper now exposes `main_grad` while preserving an existing `False`/`True` policy and leaving an absent attribute absent. The unshard-time refresh remains in place.

The regression now invokes the real MoE preparation helper before the actual FSDP local-linear fused wgrad path. All 20 configurations pass on one GPU and on every rank of an eight-GPU run, covering the sharding/dtype matrix and two accumulation cycles. Restoring only the previous helper makes both FP32/BF16 `no_shard`/no-unit controls fail with 256/256 entries wrong and max absolute error 8, matching the lost first-microbatch contribution. The 3 hook-policy cases and 8 bit-exact replay cases also pass.

Full `TEGroupedMLP` op-fuser validation was attempted separately, but this TE build was compiled with cuBLAS 13.1 and its grouped GEMM requires 13.3+. It stopped before gradient comparison. I have made that limitation explicit in the PR: the passing numerical scope is the real MoE helper plus FSDP and TE local wgrad GEMM.

files.patch:
@@ -831,12 +831,11 @@ def _ensure_main_grad(linear_module: torch.nn.Module) -> None:
         """Expose FSDP main_grad buffers required by TE fused wgrad accumulation."""
         if not getattr(linear_module, "fuse_wgrad_accumulation", False):
             return
+        # FSDP owns overwrite_main_grad: persistent buffers must retain prior microbatches.
         for param in linear_module.parameters(recurse=False):
             get_main_grad = getattr(param, "get_main_grad", None)
             if get_main_grad is not None and getattr(param, "main_grad", None) is None:
                 param.main_grad = get_main_grad()
-            if hasattr(param, "overwrite_main_grad"):
-                param.overwrite_main_grad = True

     def _ensure_main_grad_for_fused_impl(self) -> None:
         """Expose wrapper parameter main_grad buffers before TE fused ops run."""

